# JSON5 fixtures — pre-existing intentional metadata keys (`_comment`,
# `_rfc`, `_phase`, `_scope`) survive only in JSON5; strict-JSON
# prettier rejects them. Loaded by Rust test code via `serde_json`
# with manual stripping of the metadata fields. Reformatting these
# to strict JSON would either break the metadata convention or require
# a JSON5 parser, neither of which is in scope for the lint gate.
# Per RFC-0862 R17 M3 scope discipline, Phase 3 TVs split into one
# fixture per TV (TV-5/6/7/8 each own a file). RFC-0862 v1.4 also
# added a sync-vs-data-sync benchmark split (phase1_tv_0862.json).
